Legioes inteiras foram enviadas to matar Espartaco, mas  foram facilmente derrotadas by the espirito de luta e experiencia of the gladiadores. In 71 a.C., Marco Licinio Crasso 
juntou 50.000 soldados romanos bem treinados to perseguir e derrotar Espartaco. Crasso encurralou Espartacus in the sul of the Italia, derrotando suas forcas, e matando o ex-escravo 
( o corpo de Espartaco, contudo, nunca foi encontrado ). Seis mil seguidores de Espartaco foram capturados e crucificados to the longo of the  Via Apia, a estrada de Capua a Roma.=Lentulus 
Batiatus, from Capua, must have recognized his potential, because he bought Spartacus with the intention of transforming him into a gladiator. But the fierce independence 
of a warrior is not easily tamed. In 73 BCE, Spartacus persuaded seventy of his fellow gladiators, among them Crisus, to rebel against their lord. In the revolt, Batiato was 
assassinated and the gladiators fled to the backs of the neighboring Mount Vesuvius. Betrayed, Spartacus is sold to the Romans as a slave and bought by a gladiator school. 
But fate had bigger plans for the Thracian soldier - he would become the leader of the greatest revolution of antiquity and his name would remain forever engraved on history. 
While fleeing, the group was gathering free men and many other slaves, thus becoming a large and powerful army. Gladiators spent the winter of 72 BC training the newly freed 
slaves in preparation for what is now known as the Third Servant War, with its ranks numbering as many as 70,000. Entire legions were sent to kill Spartacus, but were easily 
defeated by the fighting spirit and experience of the gladiators. In 71 BC, Marco Licinius Crassus gathered 50,000 well-trained Roman soldiers to chase and defeat Spartacus. 
